      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Star trotter GUS NZ (10) makes his first appearance since a fighting Inter Dominion final win over a similar distance here in July. Readied with three trials, winning them all, and he is good enough to overcome the 50m handicap. Owns a decent fresh record so can pick up where he left off. KEAYANG STUKA (9) has been good when beaten less than 2m as runner-up in his two outings here since a spell, the latest when off this same mark. Should be nearing his peak now. PINNIE (8) enjoyed the return to the standing start when beating KEAYANG STUKA to win last start. Goes back 10m in the handicap but strikes at 50 per cent at this longer distance. COURAGE STRIDE (6) came from this mark for a solid fourth at his most recent appearance. Exotic hope.",
